  "sourceCorrection": "Earlier handoff claimed Giant Dragonfly required its same-named five-state script. The stable scene has no root-script override and inherits Enemy; DetectEvolution only selects ordinary ChargingAttackBehavior nodes. The special script is not bound in this scene. The autostart BoostTimer has no scene connection, and generic Enemy has no BoostTimer reference. Root/scene/script hashes and these guards are in the compiler.",
  "rules": [
    "HP4+2/wave, contact1+0.85/wave, speed200+/-100px/s; HP factor1 and original translated body/hurt/contact circles.",
    "Before detection: one fixed target-relative offset inside the default200px square, zero range jitter, follows the moving target without redrawing that offset. Inclusive600px detection adds20px/s once and enables default0.3s anticipation.",
    "Normal charge: direct target position at START_SHOOT,20frame cooldown,0jitter,250px maximum range, animation speed3,0.35s rush/+700px/s,0.3s recovery. Every third shot uses55frames long cooldown plus rush duration, counter preserved across transfer.",
    "No Pursuer state, recurring self-boosts, recovery/deciding state machine or contact-reset behavior is invented from the unbound special script. Meca/Mutant attacks remain source-only."
  ],
  "interfaces": [
    "Compiled detection.wanderMode/wanderWithin select existing native Offset vs Target policy; no new World/EnemySim interface.",
    "GiantDragonfly.bindingAudit records effective Enemy script, unbound special-script hash and absent BoostTimer connection. Compiler fails if the reviewed binding changes.",
    "No Arsenal/remote/profile schema or balancing changes."
  ],
